Titan Defense Solutions, Inc. proposes a comprehensive upgrade and maintenance contract for military surveillance systems utilized by the U.S. Army’s 1st Infantry Division stationed at Fort Riley, Kansas. This contract focuses on enhancing the operational efficiency of the Advanced Tactical Surveillance System (ATSS), which is essential for real-time intelligence gathering and threat assessment.

The proposed equipment upgrades include the integration of the latest Night Vision Imaging System (NVIS) and the Drone Surveillance Technology (DST) system to improve aerial reconnaissance capabilities. The ATSS will be supported by a dedicated team of engineers and operators from Titan Defense, who will collaborate closely with Colonel Michael Anderson of the 1st Infantry Division. We anticipate a contract value of approximately $2.5 million over a 24-month period, covering equipment procurement, installation, and ongoing technical support.

